KNOWNBUG
port10.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.shared\.value == 1 \|\| main\.shared\.value == 2: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.x == 0: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The initial value of the interface variable and the one of the member of
the interface port that is bound to it are separate initial-state
constraints on two variables that are equated, which contradict each
other. The model has no initial state, and every property holds
vacuously, including p1.
